    "answer": "I don't know the date. The sources I could reach don't say when conversations started surviving an api restart. They only show that this comes from issue #23, the MongoDB-backed conversation persistence work. That work moved conversations into the database with `PersistentSessionStore`, saved at the end of each turn, and stopped the engine from deleting a conversation when the socket closes. Issue #152 covers erasing from both the database and the cache, and #194 covers the cache's age bound, with the conversation still stored. In memory notes from September 2026, #23 was still described as not on main (no `mongodb` dependency, no conversations collection). So it landed after that, but I found no merge date or commit for it.",
